commendations, Play Store, and Google Assistant. This confirms the interface modifications.\n\n\nThe identified packages reside in `/system/app/` and `/system/system_ext/` within `super.img`, confirming a customized system partition. These APKs represent core system apps, highlighting modifications for the \"liberated\" interface. Examination of these packages shows a custom launcher, file manager, app stores, and control services which provide evidence of the device's customized state.\n\n\nThe absence of Megacable's app within the system image (`super.img`) and the presence of MXL Movies and Xuper TV within the user data (`/data/app`) confirms a modified configuration. The comparison between the `super.img` system apps and user-installed apps clarifies the device's customized state. The presence of the core system apps within the `super.img` alongside the user installed applications like MXL Movies, suggests this is a custom image installed on the device.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"$superFile = \\\"c:\\\\Users\\\\andre\\\\OneDrive\\\\Desktop\\\\xview\\\\normal\\\\B866V2\\\\super.img\\\"\\n$fs = [System.IO.File]::OpenRead($superFile)\\n$bufSize = 16 * 1024 * 1024\\n$buf = New-Object byte[] $bufSize\\n$targets = @(\\\"DMC.v2.25\\\", \\\"ViettelBox_B866V2\\\", \\\"TVWall.apk\\\", \\\"AppDMC.apk\\\", \\\"DLStore.apk\\\", \\\"Hdplay.apk\\\", \\\"ControlDevice.apk\\\")\\n$found = @{}\\nforeach ($t in $targets) { $found[$t] = $false }\\n\\n$offset = 0L\\nwhile (($read = $fs.Read($buf, 0, $bufSize)) -gt 0) {\\n    $str = [System.Text.Encoding]::ASCII.GetString($buf, 0, $read)\\n    foreach ($t in $targets) {\\n        if (-not $found[$t] -and $str.Contains($t)) {\\n            $found[$t] = $true\\n            Write-Host \\\"[ENCONTRADO EN SUPER.IMG @ 0x$($offset.ToString('X'))] $t\\\"\\n        }\\n    }\\n    if (($found.Values | Where-Object { -not $_ }).Count -eq 0) { break }\\n    $offset += $read\\n}\\n$fs.Close()\\n$found.Get